WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.719
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:17.019
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:17.019 --> 00:00:24.719
Bridge | Play as a team
North/South versus East/West. Four cards make a trick; play all 13 tricks.

00:00:24.719 --> 00:00:31.019
Each player controls their own cards. This version has no dummy, doubles or redoubles. This fixed deal teaches controls, not bidding strategy.

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:38.719
Weak-hand redeal
A weak hand may request a redeal. This example declines and continues to bidding.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:45.019
At most 4 high-card points qualifies: A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1. Four initial passes also cause a redeal.

00:00:45.019 --> 00:00:54.919
Choose level and suit, then confirm
East bids 3 hearts: hearts are trumps and East/West must win at least 6+3=9 tricks.

00:00:54.919 --> 00:01:03.019
Bid higher or pass. At the same level, suits rank clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades, NT. NT means no trumps.

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:15.019
The contract is set
Three consecutive passes after a bid set the contract. The last bidder is declarer: 3 hearts here.

00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:37.019
Follow the led suit
North leads clubs. East has clubs and must choose one of the enabled club cards.

00:01:37.019 --> 00:01:55.019
On desktop, click to play. On phones, select a card then tap it again. Illegal cards are disabled. The trick winner leads next.

00:01:55.019 --> 00:02:04.919
When void, discard or trump
East has no clubs left and discards a diamond. West plays a heart trump and wins the trick.

00:02:04.919 --> 00:02:13.019
Highest trump wins; otherwise highest card of the led suit wins. Off-suit aces cannot win. You do not have to trump when void.

00:02:13.019 --> 00:03:15.019
Finish the deal | Repeated plays accelerated
Every remaining card is played legally. The bars track tricks won. Continue through all 13 even after reaching nine.

00:03:15.019 --> 00:03:24.919
Result | Compare target and tricks
East/West won nine tricks, fulfilling 3 hearts. Declarer’s team wins; North/South won four.

00:03:24.919 --> 00:03:52.896
Even one trick below the target loses. Review the trick history, then return to the room for another deal.
